WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.720
Hi everyone, my name is Sai Vennam and I'm
with the IBM Cloud team.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.470
Now, I know in previous videos we talked about
technical concepts that always relate back

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.140
to cloud-native computing in one way or another.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:16.449
Now, over the years I've seen businesses harness
those concepts to create innovative solutions

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.320
to real problems.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:24.659
In this era of Hybrid and Multicloud businesses
need a way to run containerized applications

00:00:24.659 --> 00:00:26.480
in a way that they can run anywhere.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.019
In this video I want to touch on a few of
those use cases for why a business may want

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:33.880
to use Hybrid or Multicloud.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.810
Let's start with the basic one, Cloud Scaling.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:43.420
Now, most of us are probably familiar with
this, it is one of the main reasons for adopting

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:44.420
the cloud.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.270
Now, let's say we have a flower delivery service
that is able to hit a certain bottom line

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:57.570
of users. They have on-premise infrastructure
and it can hit a certain amount of user load.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:03.260
So, visualizing this here throughout the calendar
year you can imagine that their load maybe

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.920
goes up and down in response to specific holidays.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:14.110
Now, to hit those peaks they could scale up
their on-premise architecture but that's met

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:16.810
with upfront costs and cost of upkeep.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:24.940
Now, instead we'll take advantage of cloud
that allows them to scale up in response to

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:30.220
that load and then automatically key provision
resources when they no longer need them.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.750
Now, this concept is kind of general to cloud
computing not just Hybrid or Multicloud, but

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:40.780
that brings me to my next topic and here we're
going to be talking about how it can be used

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.140
to build a Composite Cloud.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:52.590
So, essentially this is going to be applications
that are spread across multiple cloud environments.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:57.869
So, back to the flower delivery service let's
say they have an on-premise architecture that

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:01.330
allows them to run three major components
of the app.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:13.510
So, let's say they have the web UI, they have
some billing API's, as well as a rewards framework.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:20.480
Now, let's say that this service is actually
based in the EU.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:27.060
And their European customers are happy but
for their North American, or American customers,

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.500
specifically around Veterans Day or Thanksgiving
their noticing that the system is bogging

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:38.340
down and so they decide to take advantage
of a Hybrid Cloud or Multicloud architecture

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.160
by composing their application across multiple
cloud environments.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.319
So, they'll take advantage of data centers
in America and essentially they've identified

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:52.220
that although their rewards framework can
stay on-prem in their European side they want

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:59.290
to move the billing and the U. I. capabilities
over. So, they'll move just those two to a

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:05.280
cloud platform of their choice in a North
American, or American datacenter. This kind

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.810
of allows them to scale up portions in response
to say American holidays while keeping their

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:16.410
EU portions individually scaled. So, in this
example the flower delivery service is able

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:24.050
to take advantage of scaling at a global level
by using the Hybrid or Multicloud architecture.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.460
Next let's talk about the airline or travel
industry.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:33.590
So, we can first start with an example of
Modernization.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:40.650
Now, in the past we've seen that reservation
systems may have been difficult to work with

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:46.090
or you might have had to call in, but almost
all the airline companies now have a mobile

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:51.170
application. So, most of the time of actually
found that it's about in general not just

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:55.470
in the travel industry but eighty percent
of all enterprise applications are actually

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:59.260
still on-prem. This likely the case in this
industry as well.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.959
So, in this specific example, let's say they
have a reservation system that's running on-premises,

00:04:04.959 --> 00:04:10.760
but to create new experiences for their end
users, let's say they've created a mobile

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:16.329
application. That mobile app of course has
a mobile backend that's maybe running in a

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:22.600
public cloud and that in turn works with the
reservation service. So again, the mobile

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:28.030
app can hit the mobile backend that in turn
works with the reservation capabilities.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:34.100
So, in this case they modernized and new user
experiences are possible, but let's take that

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.440
a step further. Now, a source for a lot of
dissatisfaction for users is whenever their

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:43.180
flights are delayed. So, when a flight is
delayed, they may have to re-book new flights.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.620
The solution is almost always the same, the
traveler wants to get to his destination in

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.800
the easiest way possible.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.560
So, what airline industries have been doing
is taking advantage of the cloud to create

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.820
maybe a recommendation feature.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:03.210
So, it allows them to book new flights as
soon as the delay is recommended or as soon

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:08.570
as the delay has ocurred and that's going
to connect up to the mobile back in service

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.009
allowing users to be able to book flights
through their phone the second the flight

00:05:12.009 --> 00:05:16.520
is delayed. This not only improves the bottom
line for the airline industry but leads to

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:20.900
happier users. So, that's one way that modernization
has been done.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:28.630
Next, let's take it even a step further and
talk about Data and AI.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:34.240
For Data and AI, the airline industry has
been taking advantage of lots of historical

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:39.060
data. So, over the decades that a company
has been around, let's say they have historical

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:43.889
data of when unplanned maintenance has happened
on their airline.

00:05:43.889 --> 00:05:49.090
In fact, thirty percent of all delay time
in that in the airline industry is actually

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.950
when unplanned maintenance happens.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:55.950
So, by taking advantage of let's say machine
learning or AI capabilities, they could hook

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:03.000
into all of the legacy data that they have,
large volumes and connect them up to machine

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.500
learning and AI capabilities.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:10.760
This allows airline industries to take advantage
of predictive analytics and get insights before

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:15.870
errors, or before that unplanned maintenance
ever occurs. This again improves their bottom

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:21.040
line, leading to happier users and a more
efficient airline industry.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:27.180
Now, today we talked about four major use
cases for Hybrid and Multicloud platforms.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:32.451
So, Cloud Scaling and Composite Cloud in the
flower delivery service, as well as Modernize

00:06:32.451 --> 00:06:34.640
and Data and AI for the airline industry.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:35.640
Now, we really have only started to scratch
the surface of the number of use cases for

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.640
why you want to use a Hybrid or Multicloud
platform.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:40.860
Now, if you like this video or have any questions
be sure to drop a like or a comment below.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.979
Be sure to subscribe and stay tuned for more
videos like this in the future.

